WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.140
Sonic hedgehog patterns the bottom of the tube.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.840
What tells the top of the tube it is the top?

3
00:00:09.833 --> 00:00:11.273
Recall neural induction.

4
00:00:12.213 --> 00:00:16.173
In frog animal caps, blocking BMP let the cells become neural.

5
00:00:17.233 --> 00:00:19.993
Now, inside the tube, BMP comes back.

6
00:00:20.813 --> 00:00:23.073
It arrives from the skin and from the roof plate.

7
00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:30.267
BMPs, bone morphogenetic proteins, act through receptor kinases and Smad proteins.

8
00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:37.287
In 1995, Karel Liem, Thomas Jessell and colleagues tested them on chick neural plate

9
00:00:37.287 --> 00:00:38.287
explants.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:44.640
BMP4 and BMP7 could mimic the dorsalizing effect of epidermis.

11
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:51.380
In 1997, they proposed that BMPs from the epidermis induce the roof plate.

12
00:00:52.383 --> 00:00:56.003
The roof plate then becomes a second source of related signals.

13
00:00:57.067 --> 00:01:00.227
It also makes Wnts, including Wnt1 and Wnt3a.

14
00:01:01.217 --> 00:01:04.697
The dorsal tube makes six early classes of interneurons.

15
00:01:05.457 --> 00:01:08.377
They are named dI1 to dI6, from the top down.

16
00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:14.607
Predict. Remove the roof plate early in a mouse, leaving the floor plate and

17
00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:15.607
notochord untouched.

18
00:01:16.507 --> 00:01:17.507
Which classes are lost?

19
00:01:23.867 --> 00:01:29.127
In 2000, Kevin Lee, Paula Dietrich and Thomas Jessell removed the roof plate

20
00:01:29.127 --> 00:01:30.127
genetically.

21
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.650
The three dorsal-most classes later failed to form.

22
00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:37.730
The classes further down did not depend on it, in that experiment.

23
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.400
The two systems also oppose each other.

24
00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.520
BMP signaling alters the response to Sonic hedgehog.

25
00:01:46.483 --> 00:01:50.103
So the wall sits between a signal from below and one from above.

26
00:01:51.263 --> 00:01:52.843
Cells in the middle can be shaped by both.

27
00:01:53.833 --> 00:01:58.053
This lesson follows the ventral code in full and the dorsal one in outline.

28
00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:00.313
Now the whole rule.

29
00:02:00.313 --> 00:02:02.473
The neighbours supply a slope.

30
00:02:02.473 --> 00:02:04.733
The progenitors draw the lines.

31
00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:08.187
Signals from below and above set the level.

32
00:02:09.047 --> 00:02:13.347
The cells read it, and how long it lasts, and answer with a combination of factors.

33
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.400
In the ventral tube, pairs of neighbouring factors repress each other.

34
00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:23.660
That helps each cell settle on one identity and hold it, though a lasting change in

35
00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:25.200
signaling can still move it.

36
00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:27.393
Keep the limits too.

37
00:02:28.533 --> 00:02:29.813
Sharp is not the same as accurate.

38
00:02:30.713 --> 00:02:32.153
The signal shapes its own slope.

39
00:02:32.993 --> 00:02:35.093
And the floor plate follows partly different rules.

40
00:02:36.183 --> 00:02:37.563
One more role waits.

41
00:02:38.463 --> 00:02:41.823
Later, the same floor plate becomes a target for growing axons.

42
00:02:42.833 --> 00:02:47.233
The takeaway: two slopes, read by the cells, become the map of the spinal cord.
